      "area": "Photovoltaic laminate",
      "actualSourceObservation": "All 24 cell instances on each wing had no contact with a supporting part; their rear faces were 0.003999999 model units ahead of the chassis. The eight conductor bars on each wing joined one another but had no supporting contact outside that grid; their rear faces were 0.003000002 ahead of cell fronts.",
      "resolution": "A seated continuous bonding sheet supports the cells and lowered conductor grid."
    },
    {
      "area": "Dish brace",
      "actualSourceObservation": "The secondary brace contacted the first brace and upper gimbal, but its housing end at service-local [5.49,0.36,0.6] did not contact the foot, hull or engine jacket. The nearest structural surface was 0.054954 from the endpoint center against rod radius 0.043.",
      "resolution": "Two clevis arms now start on a hull-seated mounting face and carry an axle connected to the reflector hub."
    },
    {
      "area": "Engine throat closure",
      "actualSourceObservation": "The radius-0.419 dark closure cylinder had no supporting contact. Rays into the actual nozzle gave radial clearances from 0.016908 to 0.022949 over the cylinder depth.",
      "resolution": "The revised closure reaches the nozzle wall; finite radial probes verify that no detached annular gap remains."
    },
    {
      "area": "Existing connected components",
      "actualSourceObservation": "Original solar root rods, bearing collars, tip hinges, chassis/frame/corners and dish rim/back hub/feed stays had real contacts. The old inner bronze nozzle ring also contacted the nozzle.",
      "interpretation": "Those revisions are design/assembly-clarity choices; this audit does not describe every replaced component as floating."
    }
  ],
